# NextAuth Integration Rules

## Setup
- Install `next-auth` via npm or yarn.
- Create a dynamic API route at `pages/api/auth/[...nextauth].js` (or `.ts`).

## Configuration
- Import NextAuth and required providers (e.g., GitHub, Google).
- Export NextAuth configuration as the default export.
- Configure providers using environment variables.

## Environment & Security
- Store sensitive keys (e.g., clientId, clientSecret) in environment variables.
- Validate environment variables on startup.
- Protect API routes by checking session validity.

## Session & Callbacks
- Choose a session strategy (JWT or database sessions).
- Customize callbacks for session, JWT, and sign-in as needed.
- Implement error handling in all callback functions.

## Client-Side Integration
- Use the `useSession` hook from `next-auth/react` for accessing session data.
- Utilize `signIn` and `signOut` functions for authentication flows.
- Handle loading and error states in UI components.

## Testing & Maintenance
- Test the complete authentication flow end-to-end.
- Regularly update NextAuth and its dependencies.
- Consult the [official documentation](mdc:https:/next-auth.js.org/getting-started/example) for updates and best practices.
